=== entry 49c8cf6d4a92
kind: translation
rules: invoke
intent: The hand-off tells the user what to type to bring the verification back in line, so that skill gets its Codex form. Everything else stays verbatim.
--- upstream
Tell the user what you verified, which tool you used and why, the bounds, what the check found in plain words, how to run it, and what it does not cover. Suggest a second target only if you found a close one. Point the user at `/maintain-formal-verification-skill` for bringing the verification back in line after changes that did not recheck it.
--- patched
Tell the user what you verified, which tool you used and why, the bounds, what the check found in plain words, how to run it, and what it does not cover. Suggest a second target only if you found a close one. Point the user at `/maintain-formal-verification-skill` (`$maintain-formal-verification-skill` in Codex) for bringing the verification back in line after changes that did not recheck it.

=== entry 04a3d939b678
kind: translation
rules: invoke
intent: The generated skill tells the next agent to read TLA+ results with the statechart skill, named in bold with no slash, keeping the sibling link. Keep refer-by-name and copying none of its commands, options, or paths.
--- upstream
If the check is a TLA+ model, tell the next agent to read every result with the pstack [`/statechart`](../statechart/SKILL.md) skill. It shows each invariant violation the checker finds as its shortest path in plain words. When the check passes, `/statechart` draws a chart of how the system moves between states. Refer to `/statechart` by name. Its commands, options, and file paths change between releases and machines, so copy none of them into the generated skill or its scripts.
--- patched
If the check is a TLA+ model, tell the next agent to read every result with the pstack [**statechart**](../statechart/SKILL.md) skill. It shows each invariant violation the checker finds as its shortest path in plain words. When the check passes, the **statechart** skill draws a chart of how the system moves between states. Refer to the **statechart** skill by name. Its commands, options, and file paths change between releases and machines, so copy none of them into the generated skill or its scripts.
